+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes cancellation or answers a member who cannot cancel a pantry order. The cutoff closes app
+cancellations when packing starts, two hours before pickup. Late cancellations had left packed bags of fresh food
+unused, even after a reminder banner asked members to cancel earlier.
+
+## Cutoff
+
+A member can cancel only before the start of their pickup slot minus two hours. At that instant and afterwards,
+cancellation is refused. For a 17:00 pickup, a cancellation before 15:00 is allowed; one at 15:00 or later is refused.
+The eligibility check is [`can_cancel`](../../larder/cancellation.py).
+
+## Why packing sets the cutoff
+
+Volunteers had found packed bags left on the shelf for three Saturdays in a row, including nine bags containing
+milk, bread and greens on October 6. Members were cancelling at 16:50 for a 17:00 pickup, after packing. A banner
+had been in place since summer, but 25 bags of fresh food had already been thrown away that October.
+
+The packing shift starts two hours before each pickup slot. Cancellations before packing cost no bag; later ones
+waste a packed bag. The cutoff follows that shift start, as agreed in [issue 31](../../notes/issue-31.md).
+
+## After the cutoff
+
+A member who cannot come after the cutoff calls the pantry; volunteers decide how to handle the request. The
+agreement in issue 31 requires the pantry's phone number in the refusal message.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The repository contains the eligibility check but no refusal-message implementation or pantry phone number, so it
+does not establish that the agreed message is displayed. When implementing or checking that message, obtain the
+pantry's contact number and include it so members can use the phone fallback.
